      "created_at": "2016-11-05T15:10:54Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-11-05T15:10:54Z",
      "body": "No, all of the other channels are able to pass their data through, they act as a proxy which takes care of transport and translation but no storage.  The DirectLine channel on the other hand is acting as a store and forward service, aka, you have a mobile app which is started up and connects to a conversation to get the latest messages from the conversation.  This requires the data to be stored in an intermediate server awaiting a client to ask for it.\n\nWe are looking at ways that we can have directline store the data in dev controlled location, but as of now we don't support it.\n\nI believe we store the data encrypted in our storage layer, and I don't know what the expiration but I know the data does expire (I think it is 7 days)\n",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
